{"t": 388.78, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FBR_Zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails S2 and S4 due to the diode voltage drop (approx 0.5V) being too significant when the piezo's open-circuit voltage is low (especially in S4 where Voc_peak is ~1.9V). Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) is implemented by adding an inductor and a switch across the piezo to flip the voltage at its extrema, effectively boosting the voltage available to the rectifier. A Zener diode (DZ33) is added to the output to clamp the voltage to 3.3V, preventing the overvoltage failure seen in S3. A storage capacitor is used to minimize ripple and stabilize the mean output for S5.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FBR_Zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails S2 and S4 due to the diode voltage drop (approx 0.5V) being too significant when the piezo's open-circuit voltage is low (especially in S4 where Voc_peak is ~1.9V). Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) is implemented by adding an inductor and a switch across the piezo to flip the voltage at its extrema, effectively boosting the voltage available to the rectifier. A Zener diode (DZ33) is added to the output to clamp the voltage to 3.3V, preventing the overvoltage failure seen in S3. A storage capacitor is used to minimize ripple and stabilize the mean output for S5.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id":